{"title":"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #15</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) (page does not exist)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #12</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A public holiday is always celebrated on the third Wednesday of a certain month. In that month, the holiday cannot occur on which of the following days?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f0607e32579cf646da6e2fec6d8d312db4df24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 16^{\\text{th}} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 22^{\\text{nd}} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 18^{\\text{th}} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 19^{\\text{th}} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 21^{\\text{st}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"463\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the first Wednesday is on the first day of the month, then the third Wednesday will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days after that, and would be in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097078d8a659ca86b7e2e2591a9ef82d731e52b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{\\text{th}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> day. \n</p><p>If the first Wednesday is on the seventh day of the month, then the third Wednesday will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days after that, and would be in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8d8c2e527481aa488a0b8963687fbbb968ba1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21^{\\text{st}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> day.\n</p><p>From this, we can realize that the holiday would have to occur between the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097078d8a659ca86b7e2e2591a9ef82d731e52b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{\\text{th}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> day and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8d8c2e527481aa488a0b8963687fbbb968ba1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21^{\\text{st}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> day (inclusive). Of the answer choices, the only one that doesn't match this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fdaf9e646c99d4859f781060001eeb21e3b798a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 22^{\\text{nd}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"82\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbod